# Golden fixtures are the exception, and the negation goes in BEFORE the first one
# is written rather than after.
#
# `render-parity` (Phase 2) proves preview and export produce identical frames, and
# `export-basic` needs media to export. Both mean committed fixtures under `Core/Tests/`.
# Without these negations that fails in the quiet direction: `git add` reports
# nothing, the file is present on the machine that made it, and the suite is green
# locally and vacuous everywhere else. The vacuous-pass guards this project already
# writes are then the only thing standing between that and a false green — which is
# exactly the failure mode `AGENTS.md` records under "a measurement that counts
# something must first assert it counted anything".
#
# Scoped to the package's `Tests/` on purpose: a stray recording anywhere else stays ignored.
# `Core/` since the package moved out of the repository root.
!Core/Tests/**/*.mov
!Core/Tests/**/*.mp4
!Core/Tests/**/*.gif

